	<!-- Ads. See iosApp/iosApp/Ads.swift and CLAUDE.md.

	     GADApplicationIdentifier below is Google's PUBLIC SAMPLE iOS application id, and it is
	     both a placeholder and a sentinel. A missing or malformed value makes
	     MobileAds.shared.start raise GADInvalidInitializationException, so something valid has to
	     be committed for the PR simulator build, which has no secrets. SplitCruiserAds.isEnabled
	     tests for exactly this value: while it is here the app draws no ad slot at all. The
	     release workflow overwrites it from the ADMOB_IOS_APP_ID secret.

	     The two unit ids are empty on purpose — empty means "use Google's test unit". They are
	     iOS-specific: an AdMob ad unit belongs to one app, and requesting an Android unit id from
	     an iOS app returns no fill rather than an error. -->
	<key>GADApplicationIdentifier</key>
	<string>ca-app-pub-3940256099942544~1458002511</string>
	<key>SCAdBannerUnitId</key>
	<string></string>
	<key>SCAdFeedUnitId</key>
	<string></string>
	<key>NSUserTrackingUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Split Cruiser uses this to show ads that are relevant to you. Rides, prices and messages work exactly the same either way.</string>
